1
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:07,110
{\pos(424,410)}~Paris - France~

2
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,480
This is useless.

3
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:14,570
They said we can't take photos or do interviews.

4
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:20,450
What kind of training are the French youth doing, closing the door on journalists?

5
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,670
What are they hiding from us?

6
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:25,710
Misaki!

7
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:27,710
Fischer.

8
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,880
You want to get in, don't you? Follow me.

9
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:34,010

10
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:36,510
We're using this secret passage.

11
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:38,970
This way, Misaki.

12
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,010
Okay.

13
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:50,270
{\an8}CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC{\an}

14
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:16,400
{\an8\pos(684,770,309)}Episode 5\NAnother Talented Player

15
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:19,360
Hey, look who's playing against the French youth!

16
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:23,580
They're French Ligue 1 professionals!

17
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:27,040
That's why they weren't letting anyone in.

18
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:29,370
That's El Sid Pierre.

19
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:30,580
Amazing!

20
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:34,840
Even against professionals, he does everything with ease.

21
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:37,090
Pierre.

22
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:44,720
Nice.

23
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,310
Hey, you'd better be careful, kid.

24
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:50,810
Juggling the ball up the stairs is dangerous.

25
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:55,320
It's fine, the ball is my friend and I'm used to it now.

26
00:02:56,030 --> 00:02:57,440
Who is he?

27
00:02:57,530 --> 00:02:58,900
Don't you recognize him?

28
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:04,700
He's Taro Misaki, the incredibly talented Japanese footballer.

29
00:03:05,330 --> 00:03:07,750
Many clubs wanted to sign him.

30
00:03:07,830 --> 00:03:10,410
But for some reason, he turned them all down.

31
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:31,600
Watch out!

32
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:38,650
Why did you do that?

33
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:39,690
Oh.

34
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:42,490
You're Taro Misaki.

35
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,410
Huh? What's wrong, Misaki?

36
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:48,990
That...

37
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:52,620
I remember now, this guy...

38
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:58,460
He's El Sid Pierre, the French youth national player from Bordeaux.

39
00:03:59,130 --> 00:04:01,130
El Sid Pierre?

40
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:06,800
When we won the French league matches,

41
00:04:06,890 --> 00:04:10,890
I heard about you from the kids in the Seine team.

42
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:11,890
What?

43
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:14,020
About a kid named Misaki.

44
00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:15,520
In that case...

45
00:04:15,810 --> 00:04:19,400
I decided to come to Paris.

46
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:25,360
Catch.

47
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:32,750
I recognize you too.

48
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:36,170
Well done, Misaki.

49
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:38,040
He's imitating Pierre's moves!

50
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:41,920
The most talented player of the French youth,

51
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:46,300
had previously been invited to the French senior national team.

52
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,810
El Sid Pierre.

53
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:51,430
He...

54
00:04:51,810 --> 00:04:55,440
Pleased to meet you, I'm Taro Misaki from Japan.

55
00:04:57,650 --> 00:05:00,480
Since you know who I am, let's skip the talk.

56
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:02,820
No need for words.

57
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:03,820
Misaki!

58
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:05,820
Not this time.

59
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:07,530
Come on, Misaki!

60
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:09,370
Pierre is amazing too!

61
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,950
The ball hung in the air.

62
00:05:15,210 --> 00:05:16,790
They struck at the same time.

63
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:17,830
Watch out!

64
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,090
Misaki and Pierre.

65
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:29,090
Both have unique talent.

66
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:31,970
- Come on, Misaki! - Misaki!

67
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:34,560
Why are you supporting Japan?

68
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:36,810
Pierre is France's national treasure.

69
00:05:36,890 --> 00:05:38,350
Beat him, Pierre!

70
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:42,860
Like the kids in Seine said, not bad.

71
00:05:43,570 --> 00:05:46,610
The rumors were true, Pierre is great!

72
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,620
- Alright, this ball will decide it. - Okay!

73
00:05:57,670 --> 00:05:59,120
- Huh? - What!?

74
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,130
Who are you to interrupt?

75
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:08,800
You...

76
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:12,140
Misaki-kun, that jersey is yours.

77
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:13,260
What?

78
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:20,770
Taro Misaki-kun, you've been invited to the Japan youth national team.

79
00:06:21,730 --> 00:06:23,770
The Japan youth team?

80
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,230
What's going on?

81
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,320
I don't know.

82
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:29,740
In two weeks, Japan will be here, in France,

83
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:36,790
playing its first official match in the International Youth Football Tournament.

84
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:43,090
Alongside Japan, France, Germany, and other countries will send teams.

85
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:46,050
In total, from South America, Asia, and

86
00:06:46,130 --> 00:06:49,680
other European countries, 12 teams are participating.

87
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:53,720
The first International Youth Tournament is in France.

88
00:06:53,800 --> 00:07:00,770
Misaki-kun, I want you to wear the number 11 jersey and be part of the team.

89
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:06,230
But... I haven't had the chance...

90
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:08,690
A real test of skill, isn't it?

91
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:14,450
Come, let's settle this in a real 11-on-11 match.

92
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:15,700
Pierre.

93
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:20,040
I guess it was really worth coming all the way from Bordeaux to Paris.

94
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:24,080
Thanks for the information, kids from Seine.

95
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:27,960
Pierre.

96
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,130
Taro Misaki.

97
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:36,310
I was really eager to play against the German Schneider in the tournament.

98
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:40,980
But now, it seems there's another opponent I'm looking forward to.

99
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:46,770
El Sid Pierre? Europe truly is the cradle of football.

100
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:49,400
He has extraordinary talent.

101
00:07:49,530 --> 00:07:51,820
By the way, who are you?

102
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:55,910
I'm Katagiri from the Japan Football Federation.

103
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:04,000
A new jersey?

104
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:06,750
Who are you playing for this time?

105
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:11,420
I haven't decided yet whether I'll do it.

106
00:08:11,670 --> 00:08:17,050
Why? Really? Normally you go wherever you're called.

107
00:08:17,550 --> 00:08:18,510
Yes.

108
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:23,190
During these 3 years in France, I continued my football.

109
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:28,020
But I didn't join any team and didn't work with a serious coach.

110
00:08:28,650 --> 00:08:33,490
This team is different. I can't say if I'm still the same as before.

111
00:08:36,450 --> 00:08:41,540
I don't know if I can still play like I used to.

112
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:45,920
And I've been away these 3 years.

113
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:49,250
I feel like I can't catch up to their level.

114
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:55,180
Even if I'm on the team, will I be able to play with them?

115
00:08:56,590 --> 00:09:00,760
Maybe I'll just get in their way.

116
00:09:01,850 --> 00:09:05,060
Even so, I want to play football with them.

117
00:09:05,310 --> 00:09:08,810
I want to play with Tsubasa-kun and the others again.

118
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:16,160
That's why I'm here, to test my skills and myself.

119
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:18,740
Go, Bossi!

120
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:20,990
Nice, your pass was great, Pierre.

121
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:23,120
Now I'll score.

122
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:25,870
Damn.

123
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,080
- No. - So close.

124
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:30,630
He almost scored against a professional.

125
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,100
The match is over.

126
00:09:43,770 --> 00:09:47,770
I'm sorry about this, I know it was a big request.

127
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:51,360
No, no, this team is very good.

128
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:55,030
I guarantee you'll win this tournament.

129
00:09:55,360 --> 00:10:00,070
No, we still have a long way to go, we're missing something.

130
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:02,790
Misaki?

131
00:10:03,830 --> 00:10:05,450
What kind of jersey is that?

132
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:14,300
I have to test myself against the French youth to see how strong I am.

133
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:17,880
In the one-on-one with Pierre, I couldn't gauge my true ability.

134
00:10:17,970 --> 00:10:23,180
But against the French youth, I can find out.

135
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:26,140
This match will be decisive,

136
00:10:26,230 --> 00:10:30,190
it will decide whether I'll join the Japan youth team.

137
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:35,690
Come on then, French youth.

138
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:37,610
What is this kid doing?

139
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:40,070
How did he get in here?

140
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:41,570
Misaki!

141
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,790
Hurry up, guys.

142
00:10:45,870 --> 00:10:47,660
- Huh? - Pierre.

143
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:50,790
It's fine, go, get the ball from him.

144
00:10:50,870 --> 00:10:51,710
O-Okay.

145
00:10:53,210 --> 00:10:56,710
This is Misaki, alone against the French youth.

146
00:10:57,130 --> 00:11:00,220
Time to test my skills.

147
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:02,720
Fast!

148
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:03,850
Misaki!

149
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:05,390
Watch out.

150
00:11:05,470 --> 00:11:07,350
He's not an ordinary player.

151
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:16,070
I'm still good, I still have skill and speed.

152
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:22,240
Get ready, El Sid Pierre, captain of the French youth.

153
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:24,620
Now face to face with Pierre.

154
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:32,120
He's sticking to me, my dribble isn't working.

155
00:11:33,130 --> 00:11:35,380
Damn it, I can't get past.

156
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:36,960
I'll take it now, Misaki.

157
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:37,880
This way.

158
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:39,260
What?

159
00:11:39,510 --> 00:11:41,260
Pass it here.

160
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:42,630
Catch.

161
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:44,890
Nice.

162
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:47,140
Focus, let's go!

163
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:48,310
Catch.

164
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,640
Catch.

165
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:52,900
They're displaying a great combination play.

166
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:57,900
The two of them against the entire French youth team!?

167
00:11:58,070 --> 00:12:02,910
This is incredible! Just like when I teamed up with Tsubasa-kun.

168
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:05,870
He's through! Past all of them.

169
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,290
I did it!

170
00:12:11,790 --> 00:12:13,000
Misaki.

171
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:17,090
Pierre, I'm sorry for barging in suddenly.

172
00:12:17,170 --> 00:12:18,050
You?

173
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:21,550
I apologize for entering the field without permission.

174
00:12:21,970 --> 00:12:24,930
But I had to test my football skills.

175
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:31,390
And the French youth team was the only team that could help me with that.

176
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:34,560
I'm sorry for doing something like this.

177
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:40,230
So, did you figure out what you wanted?

178
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:46,120
Yes, I couldn't get past you, but I've made my decision.

179
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:52,580
Misaki, we're tied, next time we'll settle it...

180
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:55,920
Yes, next time, in a real match.

181
00:12:58,040 --> 00:13:01,170
Misaki, do you know him?

182
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:03,590
No, I don't know him.

183
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:08,970
Now watch my long shot.

184
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:14,730
What!?

185
00:13:14,810 --> 00:13:17,150
What was that!?

186
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,020
{\an8}CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC{\an}

187
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:22,990
Born: May 5, Height: 165 cm, Weight: 53 kg, Blood Type: AB

188
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:28,530
{\an8}~Bremen - Germany~

189
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:26,780
This is a warm-up match, focus.

190
00:13:26,860 --> 00:13:28,780
- Catch. - Run faster!

191
00:13:28,870 --> 00:13:30,870
{\an8}Japan team's accommodation

192
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:33,870
The training was very tough.

193
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,960
Hey, Hyuga, where are you going?

194
00:13:36,210 --> 00:13:38,040
I'm going to kick the ball around and practice shooting.

195
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:39,630
Hyuga.

196
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,670
I'm going for a run too.

197
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,880
Matsuyama.

198
00:13:44,170 --> 00:13:46,300
- I'm going too. - Me too.

199
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:50,140
Tachibana, come on, let's train.

200
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:51,970
Oh, you said goal.

201
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:53,890
Good idea! Let's go!

202
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,140
Okay!

203
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:04,610
This was their second consecutive defeat in the European matches.

204
00:14:04,690 --> 00:14:07,360
Was it from the regret of the first match defeat?

205
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:12,620
Or from the intense pressure of the power gap between them and the Europeans?

206
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:19,670
Each member of the Japan youth team immediately started their personal training with great energy,

207
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:24,420
to improve their skills for the next match.

208
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:26,670
- I'm coming. - Okay.

209
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:32,140
I have to rebuild the muscles I lost during my injury.

210
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:46,110
This is the manager, ma'am.

211
00:14:46,190 --> 00:14:48,360
Tomorrow against Munich, right?

212
00:14:48,450 --> 00:14:50,410
Yes.

213
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:52,660
Wish everyone success.

214
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:53,950
Thanks.

215
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:02,710
I wish I could be there with you.

216
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:06,710
Impossible, I can't.

217
00:15:09,130 --> 00:15:12,970
{\an8}~Munich - Germany~

218
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:12,970
Gather round, guys.

219
00:15:13,350 --> 00:15:18,930
This is Karl Heinz Schneider, he'll be playing for Munich.

220
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:20,230
Nice to meet you.

221
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:24,230
As you know, he came here from Hamburg.

222
00:15:25,570 --> 00:15:32,570
Schneider played against the Japan team in Hamburg and won 6-1.

223
00:15:34,030 --> 00:15:38,790
Guys, Schneider is watching, we can't lose, right?

224
00:15:38,870 --> 00:15:40,000
Yes!

225
00:15:40,330 --> 00:15:44,460
If Hamburg won 6-1, we'll win 7-0.

226
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:46,500
- Right, guys? - Yes!

227
00:15:47,590 --> 00:15:50,130
Don't be so sure.

228
00:15:50,510 --> 00:15:51,630
Huh?

229
00:15:52,050 --> 00:15:56,390
I'm now announcing the Japan youth team's lineup.

230
00:16:00,390 --> 00:16:07,360
{\pos(424,88)}Japan Squad:

231
00:16:00,730 --> 00:16:04,940
Forwards: Hyuga, Nitta, Tachibana Kazuo

232
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:09,360
Midfielders: Tsubasa, Sawada, Tachibana Masao

233
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:13,990
{\pos(424,88)}Japan Squad:

234
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:14,570
Defenders: Matsuyama, Ishizaki, Soda, and Jito

235
00:16:13,990 --> 00:16:18,290
{\pos(424,88)}Japan Squad

236
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:18,040
And goalkeeper, Wakashimazu.

237
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:23,000
According to the agreement with Hamburg, Wakabayashi can only

238
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:27,460
play for Japan in the International Youth Tournament in France.

239
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:29,380
Japan youth,

240
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:35,050
are playing their last match in Germany against Munich youth.

241
00:16:35,390 --> 00:16:41,060
Today, Ozora Tsubasa is starting in the first 11 for the first time.

242
00:16:42,230 --> 00:16:43,940
{\an8}Japan vs Munich

243
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,440
{\an2}So many European spectators!

244
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:50,690
{\an2}Yes, my spirits are really lifted.

245
00:16:50,990 --> 00:16:54,490
I'm finally back on the field, we can't lose.

246
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:58,660
The Japan youth can't afford to lose anymore.

247
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:04,460
The third match of the European tournament, the Japan youth team

248
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:07,460
has begun against Munich youth.

249
00:17:08,670 --> 00:17:09,710
Tsubasa-san.

250
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:13,090
Come on, Tsubasa-kun.

251
00:17:14,550 --> 00:17:19,300
I haven't played for a long time and I've never played with these guys.

252
00:17:19,890 --> 00:17:24,100
Matsuyama-kun is playing defense, and the midfield is entrusted to me.

253
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:27,350
My style of play will determine the fate of the match.

254
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:31,230
Japan's fate is in my hands.

255
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,240
Tsubasa, what are you doing?

256
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:35,240
The opponent is coming!

257
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:36,990
Tsubasa.

258
00:17:37,410 --> 00:17:39,240
What's wrong, Tsubasa?

259
00:17:39,490 --> 00:17:41,990
Why is he just standing there?

260
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,120
Alright, let's go at him.

261
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,290
Oh, he moved!

262
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,380
What!?

263
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:51,380
Tsubasa!

264
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:56,260
Tsubasa-kun, wearing the number 10 jersey, jumps over the opponent's challenges with an incredible leap!

265
00:17:56,340 --> 00:18:00,050
Yes, I can do it, there's no pain in my leg or shoulder.

266
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:05,520
Alright, let's go forward, guys!

267
00:18:05,930 --> 00:18:08,150
- Okay! - Let's go.

268
00:18:10,770 --> 00:18:16,400
Tsubasa-kun in the middle, Japan youth enter the Munich half.

269
00:18:16,570 --> 00:18:17,570
Tsubasa-san!

270
00:18:21,990 --> 00:18:23,120
What?

271
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:26,580
And we see a nice combination play between Tsubasa-kun and Sawada-kun.

272
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:29,000
We can do it, we'll get through.

273
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:34,800
They still don't know our style of play.

274
00:18:35,210 --> 00:18:38,760
Catch, here comes the Drive Shot!

275
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:47,270
Oh, that's Tsubasa-kun's powerful long shot!

276
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:48,890
Wh-what!?

277
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:50,770
What kind of shot is that?

278
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:55,530
Drawing a rainbow in the German sky! This is the famous shot of Ozora Tsubasa-kun from Japan...

279
00:18:57,190 --> 00:18:59,280
Drive Shot!

280
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,530
Goal! Japan takes the lead quickly!

281
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:07,620
Schneider, that's the one I told you about.

282
00:19:07,910 --> 00:19:12,460
He's Japan's genius footballer, Ozora Tsubasa.

283
00:19:13,750 --> 00:19:17,800
You did it, Tsubasa.

284
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,300
Amazing, Tsubasa.

285
00:19:19,590 --> 00:19:22,180
Impossible!

286
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:23,640
That shot...

287
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,810
What a wonderful curving strike on the ball!

288
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:31,770
Tsubasa-kun's shot stunned all 11 Munich players.

289
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,570
Ozora Tsubasa.

290
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:39,900
Japan is ahead by a goal for the first time in this tournament.

291
00:19:39,990 --> 00:19:41,360
Well done, Tsubasa-kun.

292
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:43,070
Good job, Tsubasa.

293
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:46,040
- Oh yeah, oh yeah Tsubasa! - Bravo!

294
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,830
Your Drive Shot is on another level.

295
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:50,080
We scored the first goal.

296
00:19:50,410 --> 00:19:52,790
The Japanese players run to each other in joy.

297
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:57,630
Anyway, Tsubasa-kun's Drive Shot was incredible.

298
00:19:58,590 --> 00:19:59,590
Tsubasa.

299
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:01,340
Hyuga-kun.

300
00:20:01,630 --> 00:20:03,430
Your shot was great, Tsubasa.

301
00:20:03,510 --> 00:20:04,350
Hmm.

302
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:10,100
You scored this goal, but next time, pass to me.

303
00:20:10,430 --> 00:20:13,850
Sure. By the way, how's your leg?

304
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:16,690
In yesterday's match against Bremen...

305
00:20:16,770 --> 00:20:20,610
You seemed injured from training so much the night before.

306
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:23,030
Tsubasa, you...

307
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,530
So you were there that night too?

308
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:28,240
What are you two talking about?

309
00:20:31,370 --> 00:20:33,250
Don't worry, Tsubasa.

310
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:38,500
Just pass to me, and I'll turn them all into goals.

311
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:41,880
Okay, I got it, Hyuga-kun.

312
00:20:42,170 --> 00:20:43,380
Let's go!

313
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:47,510
Now Munich is on the attack.

314
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:50,350
We won't lose to this ridiculous team.

315
00:20:50,430 --> 00:20:52,600
We'll make up for the goal right away.

316
00:20:52,690 --> 00:20:53,520
Yes.

317
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:58,770
Just like Hamburg and Bremen, Munich is a strong team.

318
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:03,110
Japan may have scored first, but they can't let their guard down.

319
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,910
They've gotten very serious.

320
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:10,830
Oh, Munich is displaying fast play.

321
00:21:10,910 --> 00:21:14,710
They're in front of Japan's goal, Japan youth must be careful.

322
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:15,790
Catch him.

323
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,130
They're too fast.

324
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:19,920
Score your goal, Meier.

325
00:21:20,210 --> 00:21:21,300
Okay.

326
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:22,670
Like I'd allow it!

327
00:21:23,510 --> 00:21:30,350
Oh, today defensive midfielder Matsuyama-kun intercepts the pass superbly!

328
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:31,390
What!?

329
00:21:31,470 --> 00:21:33,180
You intervened just in time, Matsuyama.

330
00:21:33,390 --> 00:21:36,690
Catch, Tsubasa, the midfield is yours.

331
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:38,000
Matsuyama-kun.

332
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,650
Okay, let's go.

333
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:42,930
Good, let's accompany Tsubasa.

334
00:21:42,930 --> 00:21:43,690
Okay.

335
00:21:44,350 --> 00:21:45,590
He's getting past with dribbling.

336
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:49,940
Tsubasa-kun, with his extraordinary individual talent, gets past the midfielders.

337
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:51,200
Nice.

338
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:54,960
The ball truly seems like Tsubasa-kun's friend.

339
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:58,240
It moves as if glued to his foot.

340
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,210
Tsubasa.

341
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:08,020
So this is Ozora Tsubasa?

342
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:50,650
{\an8}NEXT EPISODE\NREFEREE! JAPAN YOUTH!{\an}